  "releaseNotes": "1.3.0: Several consume attributes on one consumer are merged into one dependency list, an unread dependency is reported as DM0036 with a code fix, and every diagnostic points at the source the reader has to change.\n      1.2.1: Code fixes no longer reformat the surrounding code; a fix changes only the text it is responsible for.\n      1.2.0: SingletonDIStartupData for passing external values to providers during initialization, and one initialization per process.\n      1.1.0: Roslyn 4.8 compatibility, deterministic packaging, and runtime lifecycle hardening.\n      1.0.0: First version",
